.DS_Store
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj
DerivedData/
dist/

# Local reverse-engineering scratch — never committed. Contains the vendor's decompiled
# code, firmware/FPGA blobs, and the codec binary (their IP). Our own clean-room protocol
# specs live in docs/. Keeping this fully local keeps the repo clean-room and publishable.
reverse/

# VSDD factory worktree (lives on the factory-artifacts orphan branch)
.factory/

# Brownfield-ingest source copies (re-derivable; see .factory/reference-manifest.yaml)
.reference/

# Generated coverage report (uploaded to Codecov in CI)
coverage.lcov

# Signing-key guard — the Sparkle EdDSA private key lives in the login Keychain and must
# NEVER be committed. These patterns stop an accidental `generate_keys -x` export (or any
# stray key/cert material) from being staged. The public key (SUPublicEDKey) is safe and
# lives in packaging/Info.plist. See docs/UPDATES.md.
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
*private*key*
*_key.txt
sparkle_*key*
eddsa_*
